Description: Fix systemd unit keys and ExecStart for Debian layout
 Two adaptations of the upstream unit for the Debian packaging:
  - StartLimitIntervalSec/StartLimitBurst belong to the [Unit] section;
    in [Service] they are ignored (and warned about) by systemd 255.
  - The daemon is installed to /usr/bin/ub_turbo_exec in the Debian
    package (FHS), not /opt/ubturbo/bin. RPM keeps its own path because
    this patch is only applied by dpkg-source in the deb source tree.
Author: Debian Packager
Last-Update: 2026-09-11

diff --git a/build/rpm/ubturbo.service b/build/rpm/ubturbo.service
index 8dc1726..bf744d6 100644
--- a/build/rpm/ubturbo.service
+++ b/build/rpm/ubturbo.service
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ After=network.target
 Type=simple
 User=ubturbo
 Group=ubturbo
-ExecStart=/opt/ubturbo/bin/ub_turbo_exec
+ExecStart=/usr/bin/ub_turbo_exec
 Restart=on-failure
 StartLimitInterval=10s
 StartLimitBurst=5
